# rfc-test-change-approved: 2026-08-07 Thomas ruled for a daemon-side shared-subnet check --
# ze evaluates RFC 2545 Section 3 itself at the producer instead of treating the operator's
# `local-link-local` leaf as the decision, and he accepted that this changes behavior for an
# operator whose leaf is set on a non-shared subnet. This enrolment is UNCOMMITTED and was
# held back because two reviewers found it published a claim the code did not meet, so these
# fixtures were never proof of a shipped claim. No assertion is weakened: the pair now
# differs in ONE variable (the route's next hop) with the same leaf and the same capability
# in both configs, so it discriminates on the Section 3 condition rather than on the leaf.
#
# rfc-test-change-approved: 2026-08-16 Thomas, extending the answer he gave on 2026-08-15 to
# the fixtures that sweep missed. The route's next hop was ::1 and the peer was ALSO ::1, so
# the fixture asserted the wire form of a message RFC 4271 Section 5.1.3 forbids ze to send,
# and originatedNextHopIsPeerOwn (forward_next_hop.go) withheld the route. The next hop moves
# to fd00::2 and the peer stays ::1. No assertion is weakened and no polarity moves: all four
# requirements below are asserted exactly as before, on a 32-octet Next Hop field whose length
# octet is still 0x20, because both halves of Section 3 hold for fd00::2 as they did for ::1.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-1 positive -- the Next Hop field carries the global IPv6
# address first and the link-local address second. The asserted MP_REACH_NLRI is 800E36
# 0002 01 20, then FD000000000000000000000000000002 (fd00::2, the route's next hop), then
# FE800000000000000000000000000001 (fe80::1, the session's link-local). Order is pinned by
# offset, so a swapped pair fails.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-2 positive -- the Length of Next Hop Network Address octet is
# 0x20 (32) because a link-local address is also included in the Next Hop field.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-3 positive -- both halves of the Section 3 condition hold. The
# speaker shares a locally connected subnet with the entity named by the global next hop
# (fd00::2/128) and with the peer the route goes to (::1/128). ze evaluates that condition against the
# host interface table; the `local-link-local fe80::1` leaf supplies the address, it does
# not decide inclusion.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-4 negative -- the "in all other cases" branch does not fire
# while the inclusion condition holds. The field is not reduced to the global address
# alone, and the length octet is not 16.
#
# Pairs with conf-llnh-lla-only.ci, which carries the SAME `local-link-local fe80::1` leaf
# and the same capability, and differs in one variable only: its route's next hop sits on
# no locally connected subnet.
option=file:conf-llnh-update.conf
option=bind:ipv6
# rfc-test-change-approved: 2026-08-16 Thomas -- the two lines below carry the next-hop move
# from ::1 to fd00::2 that the header block records. Only the 16 global octets change; the
# 0x20 length octet, the fe80::1 half, the NLRI and the 005E message length all stand.
1:cmd:announce ipv6 unicast 2001:db8:1::1/128 next-hop fd00::2 origin igp local-preference 100
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:005E02:000000474001010040020040050400000064800E3600020120FD000000000000000000000000000002FE800000000000000000000000000001008020010DB8000100000000000000000001
1:cmd:announce eor ipv6 unicast
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:001E02:00000007900F0003000201
